    "done_when": "Context: the process-global support clip mode (nova/equilibrium/forward_operator.py _SUPPORT_CLIP_MODE, set_support_clip_mode and support_clip_mode) is being retired. The certificate hub benchmarks/solovev_certificate.py migrated at 30b49fbe4: its helpers take an additive clip_mode keyword whose default None keeps the prior behaviour, and its internal set-and-restore pairs became explicit threading through ForwardFluxOperator.with_clip_mode and ForwardSolveRequest(clip_mode=...). This node migrates the ten helpers that other benchmarks import, in the same way: oracle_start_newton_probe, plasma_cell_terminal_state, plasma_cell_fixed_point_attribution, plasma_cell_trip_panels, plasma_cell_first_step_directions, plasma_cell_map_fidelity, exact_clip_seed_amplitude, exact_support_floor_attribution, unit_amplitude_current_census and fixture_positional_stiffness. Rules: (a) every set-and-restore of the global becomes explicit threading of that mode to each operator, profile and request built inside, so that no global is set; where a solovev_certificate helper is called, pass its clip_mode keyword; (b) every helper in these files that another file imports and that builds an operator, profile or request gains clip_mode: str | None = None, where None keeps today's behaviour exactly; (c) existing call signatures stay valid, so changes are additive keywords only; (d) a receipt that records a mode records the solving operator's mode, never support_clip_mode(). Gate, logged under the run directory: (1) grep finds no set_support_clip_mode or support_clip_mode in the ten files; (2) the shared interpreter /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python compiles each file with py_compile; (3) every test module that imports any of the ten files, run with JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu and -m 'not slow' in one fresh pytest process per file in place on this fleet allocation, adds no failure against the dispatch base. Compare by test id, and record baseline_suite and after_suite with 